  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 18 actions (src/actions.ts, ActionId enum, one object returned by GetActionsList) and 2 boolean feedbacks (src/feedback.ts). Nothing is generated per device model.",
    "Protocol: PandorasAutomation (PBAU packets) over a TCP socket to port 6211 (src/constants.ts PR_PORT, src/client.ts). Connection config: host (Regex.IP), domain (Regex.NUMBER, default \"0\") and a debug traffic checkbox (src/config.ts). Variables and presets are not catalogued (src/variables.ts, src/presets.ts).",
    "Sequence dropdowns (id seq or sequence) use allowCustom and, on some actions, an additional regex /^\\d+$/ (recorded in regex). The choices come from the sequence list read from the device at runtime, so they are described in choicesNote and checked through valueType/valuePattern. The source comments say a custom sequence id arrives as a string, so numeric ids (choice ids, default 1) and numeric strings both occur.",
    "The Transport, SMPTE mode, direction, ignore, mode and curve dropdowns set disableAutoExpression: true.",
    "The Sequence Opacity Fade action scales the percent value to the device range 0-65535 (SEQUENCE_OPACITY_MAX, src/constants.ts, \"confirmed empirically on hardware\" per the source comment).",
    "Upgrade scripts (src/upgrades.ts): the removed global feedback transport_state is converted to sequence_transport_state for sequence 1 (3.1.2); remaining_threshold without a sequence option gets sequence 1 (3.1.6).",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~2.1.3: option values may be expressions."
  ]
